I ran X + fvwm + emacs + netscape fine in 8MB, and I have several
machines with 64 and 128MB that run X + xfce + a couple of apps just
fine.  You don't want to open a ton of tabs in your firefox, but 128MB
is plenty for more minimal X sessions and is even fine for Gnome and
KDE if you're careful about what you run (and nethack with tiles is
well within the bounds of "careful" as long as you don't have a ton
else going on at the same time.).

If you ran X + nethack with tiles without anything else, the machine
wouldn't break a sweat.


